      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-12-22_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <p>CHESHIRE CuUNTY COUNCIL EDUCATiON DEPARTMENT. GRANTS IN AID OF TRAVELLING EXPENSES TO PUPILS ATTENDING AT PUBLIC SECONDARY SCHOOLS. The Education Committes are prepared, under certain conditions, to consider applications from parents for the payment of fares on account of pupils from the Administra- tive County, residing not Iris than three miles from approved Public Secondary Schools within the County of Chester, and who are either attending or proposing to attend ouch Schools, Copies of the conditions and forms of application may be obtained from the Director of Education, County Education office, City-road. ~.Thester.</p>
        <p>J. H. HOWITT, Acting Director of 'Wooslion.</p>
        <p>December 10th, 1906._ COUNTY OF CHESTER, TO WIT. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will be holden at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, in and for the said County, on SIORDAY,the 31st day of December, 1906, at half-past Eleven o'clock In the forenoon, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing ot all Appeals arising within the Hundaeds of Eroxton, Ifilddisburv. Nantwlch, and Wirral, forming the I Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Hundreds will take piece at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Jury for the Chester District must be In attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the opening of the Court on Morrpay. the 31st day of December, 19060 at half- past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE Court will be Adjourned to the Court Rouse. Knut,- ford, on WEDNESDAY, the 2nd day of January, 1907, at Eleven o'clock In the Forenoon. The hearing of Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Bucklow. Macclesfield. and Northwlch, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Hundreds will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Jury for the Knutsford District must be in atten- dance at the Court House, Knutsford, at the opening of the Coed on WEDABSD•Y. the 2nd day of January, 190 T. at 'Eleven o'clock In the porenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. I Chester, 11th December, 1906,</p>
