        <p>Mr. Owen Muldowney, a furniture remover, of 15, Church-road. Seacombe, said to a newspaper reporter: —" lam seventy-nine years of age, and up to last. spring I never knew a day's illness. Then I was suddenly seized with disagreeable pains which seemed to shoot through my whole body. Many a day I lay in helpless agony on the bed, racked with pains from head to foot. It seemed impossible to get rid of the pain, no matter what I did, but at last I decided to try Zam-Buk. My son gave me a sound rubbing with the balm all over my body, and by next morning I was con- siderably relieved. My son continued to rub Me with Zara-Link, obeying the injunction to "rub it in" right heartily, and in a very short time I was completely cured. lam never without a box of Zarn-lluk now, and have often proved its usefulness for injuries." Rubbing Zam-Buk in is the surest way to rub pair. out. It is unequalled as an embrocation for sore throat and chest, stiff neck, chill, cold-pains in limbs,. joints, or back; and cures chapped hands, chilblains, eczemd, scalp diseases, pimples' boils, ulcers, piles, chafing, festering, cuts scalds, ,kn. Price is. id. or 2s. Pd. per box (2s. Pd. box contains nearly four -times the Is. 1.W.)</p>
