        <p>"My life was happy enough until I reached my seventeenth year," said Miss Marie Stephenson, of Pinder's-yard,Norton, Doncaster, "then the future was blackened by a terrible cloud.Anmmia gained such a hold on me that I became an object of pity and sympathydf finally I had not found new blood and renewed energy in Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, I dread to think what would have become of me. "At first a heavy, tired feeling came over me. With this languor I, lost all appetite, and mother was alwais saying, Why don't you eat ? ' but I felt that I had not Arength to masticate solid food,and everything I took, even a cup of weak tea, gave me the most dreadful pains in the chest and stomach. I began to avoid com- pany. After a short walk I have dropped on the couch half fainting with exhaution. Pains all up my back and across my shoulders, with a continual gnawing ache in my legs and feet made life miserable. Mother had often to help me to bed because of my weakness. "As time went on I could not do a thing to help mother, and soon was too weak even to help myself. Tired and helpless in limb and body, and racked with tortures, some mornings I would creep down to break- fast only to sink into a chair panting for breath. The mere smell of food would turn me against it. My eyes were sunken and I lost flesh and weight,vvhile my cheeks grew pinched and colourless, and my features drawn with pain. Numerous tonics and medicines were tried, but I gained no benefit from them. At last a friend who called said to my mother, 'The girl is terribly anwmic. Mrs. Stephenson.' The truth flashed , upon us, and I told mother that Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People had cured hundreds of girls of anTmia, and would curb me. Very soon afterwards I obtained a box, and because I took half the contents without any apparent relief I began to lose faith, and fancied that the old experience of failure would be repeated. But judge of my surprise when after going on with the pills a.little longer I found that I could eat ordinary meals without pain. I really began to want food, and was SOOD eating quite like any healthy girl. Then, of course, I continued Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, and quickly got stronger. ..;," In a short time I was free from aniemia, the weak- ness was overcome, and , I never felt languid or sad. I Occasionally I felt a little faintness, and stitch ' in my side after hard exertion, so I still continued the I Pills, and it was not very I long before I became free horn all my ailments and developed properly into eal thy womanhood. my cure I have never am as happy as can be. - better to help her through life Pslls for Pale People." For languishing, suffering anannie girls and women whose one great need is New Good Blood, there is no remedy equal to Dr. Williares'Pink Pills /for Pale People, for they actually make blood. They have cured Anmmia, Indigestion,Palpitations, Rheumatism,Sciatica, Neuralgia, St. Vitus' Dance, Eczema, Nervous Dis- orders, Paralysis, Locomotor Ataxy, and Effects of Overwork or Worry, also Ladies' Ailments, But only the genuine pills cure (seven words as above). Of most dealers, or direet from the British Depot, 46, Holborn-viaduct, London, post free is. 9d. for one box, or 13s. 9d. for six.</p>
