        <p>WAEMING TON N". SANK EY.—These old rivals met on Saturday in a run from the latter club's headqnarters, both teams being fairly well represented. Trail was laid by five of Sankey, and two of Warrington over 61 miles of heavy country including several ploughed fields. Joe Riley (Sankey) soon took the lead and won some- what easily. The next to finish was another Sankey man, J. Stamps, but the race resulted in a win for War- rtngton by five points. This is a splendid performance considering Warrington lost the first two places and only the first five were counted. Result : \V ARP, INGTCYN. SANKEY. H. K. Jepson H. Holbrook S. Parsonage ......... 5 F. Mahoney 4 G. Watmough 6 A. Wiaistaker R. Bennett LANCASHIRE JUNIOR CUP.</p>
        <p>A meeting of the Lancashire County Union Com- mittee was held in Manchester on Tuesday evening, Mr. H. Ashton (Warrington) °cooping the chair. The draw for the fourth round of the Lancashire Junior Cup, to be played on the grounds of the clubs first named on February 9th, was made as follows :—Wigan Highfield v. Askam ; Rochdale Rangers or Salford St. Bartholomews's v. Egerton.</p>
