        <head>P r7NI 7 )'..k •". , J a' ,N</head>
        <p>P r7NI 7 )'..k •". , J a' ,N</p>
        <p>[ALL RIGHTS RESERVED.I</p>
        <p>WRITTEN IN SCARLET.</p>
        <p>By ALICE MAUD MEADOWS, Author of "One Life Between," "A Million of ' Money," "The Extreme Penalty," "For Love of a Lady," "I Charge You 130th," &amp;o.</p>
        <p>SYNOPSIS OF PRECEDINti CHAPTERS: It is the wedding eve of John Brandon, a well-to-do countr:, gentleman, and Celia Verde, daughter of Lr.dy Caroline Verde. Celia had been engaged to John's brother Dick, a wild and reckless young man, sub- posed to . have died abroad. Celia admits that she loved her old sweetheart better than the new—in fact, that she does not love John at all. He, how- ever, adoring her, promises himself that be will win her love after m4rriage. Then all is changed by the sudden reappearance of Dick, who meets his brother as he is going homewards. No other person has seen the Wanderer except Lady Caroline's maid, who takes him for a ghost. John Brandon lets his Brother in by•the library window, unseen by his servants. Drck laughs at the idea of John marry- ing Celia, who, he is certain, still loves himself. His careless taunts excite John to fury, a(nd be strikes his brother violently op the head with a ruler, intending only to disable him until after the wedding takes place. To his horror, however, the signs of death are manifest. With quiet resolution be places the body in a large safe. At that moment the. police arrive at the house in search of a convict who has just escaped from a neighbouring prison. They insist on examining the house, as the fugitive. has been trated in that direction. Finally they open the safe. John Brandon is in an agony bl fear. The safe is empty! Later on the convict knocks at the study•window, and Brandon admits him. He explains that in Brandon's absence he entered, opened the safe, and discovered the body, which he abstracted with the intention of changing clothes. He was disturbed by the police, and hid the body hurriedly, and is now in the darkness unable to find the place again. A better plan of safety, however, has now suggested itself. He is a gentleman born and bred; and he compels Brandon 10 introduce him to the wedding guests as Vernon Salisbury, an old friend:, who had unexpectedly turned up. The convict st•?es John's sister, Olive, and shews evident admiration, to time disgust of Paul Clifford, who loves the fair young girl, and has just been assured his love is returned.</p>
      </div>
