        <head>BILLIiRDS.</head>
        <p>BILLIiRDS.</p>
        <p>W.kBRINDTON LIBERAL CLUB v. WIDNES LIBERAL CLUB.</p>
        <p>This match was played at Warrington on Tuesday evening in the presence of a large number of members. Victory rested with the heme team, but some of the Widnes men accomplished excellent performances. P. Quinn played beautiful billiards against the local champion Marshall, and in addition to a break of 51, made two or three in the thirties. A good display was also given by H. Laws, a son of the late Mr. T. 'Laws, and he bids fair to make a class player. Scores : WARRINGTON. 'WIDNES. G. Marshall 102 P. Quinn 2OO W. Whittaker 900 J. Nain 154 J. Halliwell 123 A. Parkinson 900 E. V.Walker 157 H. Laws 2OO J. Davies l5O F. Martindale 49 W. Green l5O J. Travels 64 W. Ford 350 H. Woods 63 E. J. Mitchell l5O T. Mitchell 125 S. Jakeman l5O E. Jolley W. Patrick 150 F. Wright 125 J. Gorst 110 S. Ellis 49 A. Sanders 125 Wright 150 -- 1516</p>
