        <p>PADGATE. , WEF-,LEV GUELD.—The annual Christmas social in connection with the Padgate Wesley Guild was held in the Wesleyan School on Monday evening. The Rev. W. Mellor presided over a large audience. Mr. Harold London gave some excellent selections on the gramo- phone, after which Miss Mellor, recited with much foroe and expression. Miss Mason, of Fearnhead, sang very sweetly," Dolly's Revenge," aud Miss Florrie Bennett was applauded for her Sortg. After an interval, during which refreshments were served, several instructive and amusing competitions were held, the prize in the post-card competdioa being carried off by Mr. Arthur Ward. This was the last meeting of the guild for the half-session and members are articipating a very success- ful session in the coming. year.</p>
